Callback Hell: Asli Problem
Abhi tak sab badhiya lag raha hai na? Lekin real-world backend mein jab ek ke baad ek asynchronous kaam karne padte hain, toh callbacks dushmani par utar aate hain.

Maan lo tumhein ek user ka order process karna hai:

Pehle user check karo (Database query - Async)

Fir uske items ka stock check karo (Async)

Fir payment process karo (Async)

Fir email bhejo (Async)

Agar ye sab callbacks se karoge, toh code aisa dikhega:

/*
JavaScript
checkUser(userId, function(user) {
    checkStock(user.cart, function(stock) {
        processPayment(user.total, function(paymentStatus) {
            sendEmail(user.email, function() {
                console.log("Sab khatam!");
                // ❌ Is arrow jaise structure ko kehte hain CALLBACK HELL ya Pyramid of Doom!
            });
        });
    });
});

*/
Yeh code padhne mein aur debug karne mein narak (hell) ban jaata hai, isiliye isko Callback Hell kehte hain.

🎯 Agla Target
Is Callback Hell se bachne ke liye hi JavaScript mein Promises aur Async/Await ka janam hua tha, jo tumne file system mein use kiya tha!
